Last week, I wrote&hellip;
 I used to love this industry, and I do still love many of wonderful people in it. But as we’ve shifted from a craft to industrialization, everything I loved about the work itself has died.
 I&rsquo;m constantly wondering, &ldquo;What would I do next if I wasn&rsquo;t in tech anymore?&rdquo;
And I keep coming up short.
Trade &amp; Craft I plan to keep riding the tech train for as long as possible, but treat it like a trade rather than a personality the way folks in plumbing or carpentry do with their work.
